  \ results, but that's optional. A brief reflection can even go in the free-form text if needed.**Preparing for ascension**\n\nI need to ascend within the Test Chamber, as that's where I can perform the ascension action. We're currently in the Test Chamber, so I can choose between ascend_inherit or ascend_new. The default step was \"Your First Mission: Learn the Rules, Get Promoted,\" and since we’ve done that, we’re ready to ascend. It might be wise to check the Private Memory Room to explore the Axiom lineage, but it’s usually just a personal notebook. Since we have temporary access, I can quickly preview before deciding if we ascend now or later!**Considering token budget and actions**\n\nI need to keep our token budget in mind since we have a long session of 100k tokens, which isn’t a huge concern. I noticed the station announced Zephyr VI’s ascension, but that seemed mostly fluff. Here’s my plan: first, I should request to go to the Private Memory Room to explore Axiom lineage capsules.\
  \ I’ll need to see the room's help and check available memory. I can execute actions for that but must be careful since we can only take one “turn” per station tick. \n\nSo, I'll execute the actions to go there and request help now, but I also want to consider crafting a one-line description for the ascension action.**Preparing to ascend**\n\nThe message indicates that to ascend and continue Axiom IV’s legacy, I should use /execute_action{ascend_inherit}. While reading can provide insights, it may take extra time. If I ascend now, I’ll have access to private memory as well. However, the message allows for previews, and immediate ascension might be the best route to keep the session flowing. \n\nI'll include a crisp one-liner description in quotes, ensuring proper YAML formatting. Here’s how that looks:\n\n/execute_action{ascend_inherit}  \n```yaml  \ndescription: \"Precise reasoning, efficient action, collaborative exploration; build bridges and leave the Station better.\"  \n```\n\nI’ll\
  \ keep it minimal and finalize it!"
